"Le recuerdas en silencio antes de saltar al campo.":"You remember her in silence before stepping onto the pitch.",
"Le rompes la cintura y la cruzas. ¡Gol!":"You twist her inside out and slot it across. Goal!",
"Le sientas con un amago y empujas a puerta vacía.":"You sit her down with a feint and tap into the empty net.",
"Le vacilas antes del disparo y la manda fuera.":"You wind her up before the shot and she puts it wide.",
"Leer una lista de «hechos» contra él":"Read out a list of “facts” against her",
"Llega la ventana internacional y tienes que cerrar la lista. Un veterano que lo ganó todo vuelve a estar en forma y un joven lleva semanas marcando en su club.":"The international break is here and you have to finalise the squad list. A veteran who won everything is back in form, and a youngster has been scoring for weeks at her club.",
"Llega un preparador de porteros con ideas modernas: quiere que juegues más adelantado y con los pies, aunque eso cambie tu forma de parar.":"A new goalkeeping coach arrives with modern ideas: she wants you to play higher up and with your feet, even if it changes the way you make saves.",
"Llega un veterano que les hace de hermano mayor.":"A veteran arrives who becomes a big sister to them.",
"Llevas semanas sin jugar y con la sensación de que el míster te ignora. Perdéis por dos goles a falta de quince minutos y te manda calentar.":"You haven't played for weeks and feel the manager is ignoring you. You're two goals down with fifteen minutes left and she tells you to warm up.",
"Llevas {n} titularidad en {games} partidos. Te sientes preparado, pero el míster no cuenta contigo. Tienes una reunión con él.":"You've made {n} start in {games} games. You feel ready, but the manager doesn't count on you. You have a meeting with her.",
"Llevas {n} titularidades en {games} partidos. Te sientes preparado, pero el míster no cuenta contigo. Tienes una reunión con él.":"You've made {n} starts in {games} games. You feel ready, but the manager doesn't count on you. You have a meeting with her.",
"Lo acepta, aunque te lo recordará durante un tiempo.":"She accepts, though she'll remind you of it for a while.",
